                <pb facs="0834" n="662" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg662"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 855.48/588</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Willard</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-05-04T10:00:00+00:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 4, 1917, 10 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 10.15 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>520. Department’s 328, March 6 [<hi rendition="#italic">16?</hi>], 4 p.m.<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d940-f1"/> German Minister for Foreign Affairs states that if
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Storstad</hi> was sunk in war zone on March 8 it was
                    fault of captain who was at Saint Vincent from February 6 until end of month
                    and, therefore, must have known of declaration of war zone and nevertheless
                    ventured to enter it. Also states that so far as known ship was not provided
                    with German safe-conduct in which case vessel showed without right the
                    characteristics of the insignia of Commission for Relief of Belgians.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Willard</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
